---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Home">
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-brand-light">pi-utility-server</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-text-muted max-w-2xl">
      A homelab built, over-built, and then deliberately cut back down &mdash;
      on a single Raspberry Pi 4B. This isn't a showcase of running as many
      containers as possible. It's a record of what got tested, what got
      rejected, and why, with the reasoning kept alongside the code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">The arc</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-light pl-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-light">v1.0 — Single Pi, Compose only</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">
          Started deliberately minimal: one Pi 4B, 4GB RAM, Docker Compose. No orchestrator.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-light pl-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-light">Multi-node ambition, tested and rejected</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">
          K3s, ArgoCD, and Helmfile were evaluated for orchestration, then removed.
          K3s alone costs ~600&ndash;800MB idle RAM &mdash; too much overhead on a 4GB box
          before running a single real workload. Compose won on RAM budget, not features.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-light pl-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-light">The big offload</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">
          A second node (Windows, 16GB RAM) took on the full observability + secrets stack:
          Grafana, Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, Alertmanager, Authelia, Infisical &mdash; 11 containers,
          migrated off the Pi in sequence to keep it under a 3.5GB budget.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-light">The retirement</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">
          That full stack ran, then got switched off. Single-operator homelab, no multi-user
          access-control need, no rotation workflow ever actually used, no tracing need that
          materialized. Uptime Kuma covers what actually gets checked day to day.
          Documented as ADR-009, not silently deleted.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-light pl-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-light">Where it landed</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">
          A lean core of 8 services that get used, a single-container Netdata swapped in for
          the six-container metrics stack it replaced, and a <code class="text-brand-light">_retired/</code>
          folder pattern &mdash; nothing gets silently deleted, everything decommissioned stays
          one git command away.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">What's actually running</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-6 bg-surface-light/30">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">autobot &mdash; Raspberry Pi 4B</h3>
        <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mb-3">4GB RAM &mdash; always-on core &mdash; the only node in daily use</p>
        <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-text-muted">
          <li>Vaultwarden &mdash; password vault</li>
          <li>Gitea &mdash; self-hosted git + CI</li>
          <li>Headscale &mdash; self-hosted mesh control plane</li>
          <li>Pi-hole &mdash; DNS ad-blocking</li>
          <li>Samba + Syncthing &mdash; file storage &amp; sync</li>
          <li>Uptime Kuma &mdash; service monitoring</li>
          <li>Netdata &mdash; real-time system metrics</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-6 bg-surface-light/30">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Built, kept, not running</h3>
        <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mb-3">Configured and version-controlled &mdash; brought up only if actually needed</p>
        <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-text-muted">
          <li>Nextcloud + MariaDB + Redis</li>
          <li>Home automation stack</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-3">
          Retired entirely (Traefik, Portainer, CrowdSec, Home Assistant,
          the full Windows observability stack) live in git history, not on disk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Key Stats</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 text-center bg-surface-light/20">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-light">8</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">Live services</div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 text-center bg-surface-light/20">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-light">9</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">ADRs written</div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 text-center bg-surface-light/20">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-light">1.9</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">TB Storage</div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 text-center bg-surface-light/20">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-light">11</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1">Containers retired</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-brand">Quick Links</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-text-muted">
      <li><a href="/hub" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">Live Hub &rarr; — all services, health status</a></li>
      <li><a href="/architecture" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">Architecture diagram &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><a href="/projects" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">All projects &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><a href="http://100.64.0.1:8087/vansh/pi-utility-server" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">Gitea repo &rarr;</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
